## unused: Why was progress not made sooner?

**NOTE: IDK if we should include this section; it's incomplete atm anyway. IMO it probs comes off as condescending or otherwise bad.**

Because people weren't looking for it in the right places. They followed the wrong paths.

My personal opinion is that there are several common *errors in thinking* that have been made repeatably and reliably by those in the blockchain community. Those errors are not unique to blockchain folk; they're close to ubiquitous through scientific and technical communities.

If you are interested in understanding these errors, and improving your own thinking methods, I suggest you read:

* Goldratt's *The Choice* and his books on ToC
* Rand's *Philosophy: Who Needs It*
* Deutsch's *Fabric of Reality* and *The Beginning of Infinity* (you will not learn much if you do not read slowly)
* The essays on [fallibleideas.com](https://fallibleideas.com) (a community about learning)
* Temple's yes/no philosophy and Critical Fallibilism courses

You don't need to read those to understand this paper. They might help, but it is, like, months of reading so it would be counterproductive to expect you to read them.
